le before a perfect verb, marking the clarity as established rather than tentative — topics: certification particle fixes completed evidential clarity\n38:- 29:38:7 تَبَيَّنَ: Form V perfect of becoming clear or distinct; the evidence has self-manifested to the audience from the ruins — topics: perfect verb and broad subject make evidence already clear; Form V makes clarity emerge from the evidence itself; clarity for the audience frames failed insight in the peoples\n39:- 29:38:8 لَكُمْ: prepositional phrase routing the manifest evidence to the addressed audience as witnesses — topics: dative suffix turns audience into accountable witnesses\n40:- 29:38:9 مِنْ: source preposition that makes the dwellings the origin, medium, or sample of the evidential clarity — topics: source preposition turns dwellings into evidence-channel; attachment ambiguity remains controlled by local syntax\n41:- 29:38:10 مَسَاكِنِهِمْ: possessed plural dwelling-places governed by the source phrase; ruined habitation becomes visible evidence — topics: base source governance with variant agency pressure; dwelling-root becomes still ruin testimony; dwellings recur as the surviving witness after destruction\n42:- 29:38:11 وَ: resumptive conjunction returning from the evidence parenthesis to the causal narrative — topics: resumptive conjunction returns to causal narration\n43:- 29:38:12 زَيَّنَ: Form II active beautifying or adorning of deeds, with recipient and object separated and the agent named — topics: active verb separates agent, recipients, and object; Form II turns moral judgment into worked-over surface; beautification formula leads into path obstruction\n44:- 29:38:13 لَهُمُ: prepositional recipient phrase for beautification, ironically marking the harmed group as those for whom the deeds were made attractive — topics: benefactive-looking lām marks harmful affectedness\n45:- 29:38:14 هُمُ: bound plural pronoun carrying the named peoples forward as one affected group — topics: plural pronoun keeps one affected group across roles\n46:- 29:38:15 ٱلشَّيْطَانُ: definite nominative adversarial agent who beautifies the deeds; remoteness pressure fits the later separation from the path — topics: definite nominative subject exposes the adversarial agent; remoteness root fits distance from the path; shaytan participates in recurring beautification and obstruction formula\n47:- 29:38:16 أَعْمَالَهُمْ: their collected deeds or works as the object made attractive and the hinge toward diversion — topics: accusative plural construct gathers their practice-field; neutral action-root becomes dangerous under beautification; beautified deeds pivot into path obstruction\n48:- 29:38:17 فَ: causal-sequential particle making the obstruction follow from the beautification — topics: fa turns beautification into immediate consequence\n49:- 29:38:18 صَدَّهُمْ: completed transitive obstruction or turning-away of the named peoples from the path, without erasing the path itself — topics: attached object makes the peoples acted upon; blocking turns people away without destroying the way; causal sequence and way-collocation make diversion formulaic\n50:- 29:38:19 عَنِ: separation preposition completing the obstruction frame by marking what they are turned away from — topics: preposition supplies the away-from target of obstruction\n51:- 29:38:20 ٱلسَّبِيلِ: the definite singular way or proper course, governed after the separation preposition and targeted by obstruction — topics: definite singular path is the recognized course; genitive noun is locked under the away-from frame; path range carries course and flow pressure; path is the standard target of obstruction\n52:- 29:38:21 وَ: final conjunction that adds the closing state and, in context, makes it concessive — topics: final conjunction joins and concessively sharpens the paradox\n53:- 29:38:22 كَانُوا: past auxiliary/copular verb establishing the plural subjects in an already-held state of insight — topics: plural verb keeps the named doublet active; auxiliary plus participle marks a standing state; auxiliary-participle pattern carries into the next ayah\n54:- 29:38:23 مُسْتَبْصِرِينَ: Form X masculine plural active participle of insight, seeking, possessing, or claiming clear perception in the ayah closing — topics: accusative participle names a shared perceptual state; Form X heightens insight while keeping multiple readings open; closing insight seals the clarity-versus-failure envelope; rare participle inversely recalls the shaytan encounter; fallen bodies contrast with insight-equipped minds\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/08_surah.md-39-- 29:37 فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ ٱلرَّجْفَةُ فَأَصْبَحُوا۟ فِى دَارِهِمْ جَٰثِمِينَ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/08_surah.md:40:- 29:38 ◀ focus وَعَادًۭا وَثَمُودَا۟ وَقَد تَّبَيَّنَ لَكُم مِّن مَّسَٰكِنِهِمْ ۖ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَكَانُوا۟ مُسْتَبْصِرِينَ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/08_surah.md-41-- 29:39 وَقَٰرُونَ وَفِرْعَوْنَ وَهَٰمَٰنَ ۖ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُم مُّوسَىٰ بِٱلْبَيِّنَٰتِ فَٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا كَانُوا۟ سَٰبِقِينَ\n--\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-83-- from 29:39→29:38 (nomination, medium): Hemen onceki ayette suslenen amellerin gorur haldeki toplumu yoldan cevirmesi, odaktaki siralanmis ibret baglamini kurar.\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md:84:  - 29:38 وَعَادًۭا وَثَمُودَا۟ وَقَد تَّبَيَّنَ لَكُم مِّن مَّسَٰكِنِهِمْ ۖ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَكَانُوا۟ مُسْتَبْصِرِينَ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-85-  - **29:39** وَقَٰرُونَ وَفِرْعَوْنَ وَهَٰمَٰنَ ۖ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُم مُّوسَىٰ بِٱلْبَيِّنَٰتِ فَٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا كَانُوا۟ سَٰبِقِينَ\n--\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-322-  - **29:37** فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ ٱلرَّجْفَةُ فَأَصْبَحُوا۟ فِى دَارِهِمْ جَٰثِمِينَ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md:323:  - 29:38 وَعَادًۭا وَثَمُودَا۟ وَقَد تَّبَيَّنَ لَكُم مِّن مَّسَٰكِنِهِمْ ۖ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَكَانُوا۟ مُسْتَبْصِرِينَ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-324-\n--\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-512-\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md:513:## 99. 7:74\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md:514:- review 29:38→7:74: strong — Semud'un daglardan evler yontmasini bildirerek odakta gorunen Semud meskenlerinin insa edilmis niteligini dogrudan aciklar.\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md:515:- from 7:74→29:38 (nomination, medium): Keeps Aad and Thamud visible as an instructive aftermath of deception and ruin.\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-516-  - 7:73 وَإِلَىٰ ثَمُودَ أَخَاهُمْ صَٰلِحًۭا ۗ قَالَ يَٰقَوْمِ ٱعْبُدُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُۥ ۖ قَدْ جَآءَتْكُم بَيِّنَةٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ ۖ هَٰذِهِۦ نَاقَةُ ٱللَّهِ لَكُمْ ءَايَةًۭ ۖ فَذَرُوهَا تَأْكُلْ فِىٓ أَرْضِ ٱللَّهِ ۖ وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوٓءٍۢ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌۭ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md:517:  - **7:74** وَٱذْكُرُوٓا۟ إِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَآءَ مِنۢ بَعْدِ عَادٍۢ وَبَوَّأَكُمْ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ تَتَّخِذُونَ مِن سُهُولِهَا قُصُورًۭا وَتَنْحِتُونَ ٱلْجِبَالَ بُيُوتًۭا ۖ فَٱذْكُرُوٓا۟ ءَالَآءَ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-518-  - 7:75 قَالَ ٱلْمَلَأُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا۟ مِن قَوْمِهِۦ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسْتُضْعِفُوا۟ لِمَنْ ءَامَنَ مِنْهُمْ أَتَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّ صَٰلِحًۭا مُّرْسَلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ ۚ قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّا بِمَآ أُرْسِلَ بِهِۦ مُؤْمِنُونَ\n--\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-1311-  - 27:23 إِنِّى وَجَدتُّ ٱمْرَأَةًۭ تَمْلِكُهُمْ وَأُوتِيَتْ مِن كُلِّ شَىْءٍۢ وَلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيمٌۭ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md:1312:  - **27:24** وَجَدتُّهَا وَقَوْمَهَا يَسْجُدُونَ لِلشَّمْسِ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ فَهُمْ لَا يَهْتَدُونَ\n_commentary/v9/input/v2/s029/29_38/09_inter_ayah.md-1313-  - 27:25 أَلَّا يَسْجُدُوا۟ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِى يُخْرِجُ ٱلْخَبْءَ فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُخْفُونَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُونَ\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
